Z||000017||TOM||10-12-1999||07:33 PM||||Email me and I will reply with a picture of the vents.||||reg||1
Z||000018||Patrick||10-12-1999||07:54 PM||||<BR>Aw, come on Tom, can't you just post them here for us all to see?<P>cmyokley, the only problem with your suggestion would be if your idea somehow limited the amount of air flow through the radiator. I guess it would depend on the size of the openings in the hood. I think it would be better (and easier) to just let the air escape where it wants, out the bottom and/or out the top. Either way, the air pressure is being lessened by having the openings in the hood.<P>||||reg||4
Z||000019||lowCG||10-12-1999||10:09 PM||||Patrick,that's the approach I took,and it works great;I think the existing area behind the radiator is a decent volume the way it is.<BR>I also panelled in the opening beneath the radiator,next will be to make a panel to cover the opening behind the crossmember,although I don't expect to get the same result from this as the front panel,and 4 1/2" dam (formed on the back of the panel).||||reg||1
